'''Añãngaraçú''' (from [[W:Tupinambá language|Tupinambá]]; {{Literal translation|land of the {{W|Anhangá|great old spirit}}}}) is a [[Regions of Balisca|region]] in central [[Pindorama]], an [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|indigenous nation]] within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Its sole land border is with [[Catanduva]] to the west. It has an area of {{convert|139520.94|km2|mi2|abbr=on}} making it the largest region of Balisca. The administrative seat and most populous city of Añãngaraçú is [[Yvyra'ara]]. 

